# RECEIVED-VALUE-NOT-AN-EXPRESSION (steps/defects.md): `x: 1 2` gives the int
# place x two neighbouring values with no operator between them: not one value
# (no field captures its neighbour). A literal is no name, so no reader takes
# the line for a declaration. The common check refuses at the extra value,
# before native and walker split, as a declaration's one-value check does.
int: x 1
x: 1 2
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: x; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
